  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "OSC: Avoid tvb_get_ptr with length -1",
  "description": "Note here that calling tvb_get_ptr with length -1 and then calling\nmemchr with the _reported_ length can poke at bad memory addresses\nfor truncated packets.\n\nUse tvb_find_uint8_remaining. Make a few variables unsigned.\nOnly call tvb_get_ptr if we know we will decode, and call it\nwith the length. Calculate that length using offsets instead of\npointer arithmetic. Don't ask the TCP dissector to desegment if\nwe can't desegment.",
  "state": "merged",
